# 024 · Models into the pod, results out

**Status:** `IN_PROGRESS` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Rigs on RunPod

## What

Model weights come by URL and checksum into the pod's volume or a network volume, with progress. An optional Hugging Face token for gated models is held by the supervisor. Champions and exports leave the pod before it ends.

## Why

Quantization and engine work need large models, and a pod's disk goes away when the pod ends.

## Done when

- [x] A large model imports with progress and a checked hash.
- [ ] A terminated pod's champion is on control or in the project's results repository.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-20, owner: As recommended: results go to the project's results repository when it has one, otherwise as an upload to control.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the v0.1.0 release plan.
- 2026-10-20: Built, for every kind of rig (nothing in it is RunPod's own):
  - **Models in.** The supervisor downloads a `model` import by URL into the inbox, hashing it as it streams; a file with another SHA-256 is deleted and the assignment fails. It checks the free space first, follows redirects itself (HTTPS to HTTP refused), and keeps a broken download as `.part`, which the next try continues with an HTTP range. Progress is in the supervisor's report to control (`models`), in Live, as `model_*` steps in the rig's history, and in a **Models** row on the rig's page (`src/supervisor/model-download.ts`, `src/control/model-steps.ts`).
  - **Gated models.** `THERMITE_HF_TOKEN_FILE`, read by the supervisor only, as its other secret files; sent to `huggingface.co` and `hf.co` over HTTPS only, never after a redirect to another host, and never into the inbox, a line, the report or an error.
  - **Results out.** With a results repository, nothing changes. Without one, the supervisor sends each export to control, file by file in pieces; control checks every file against the manifest and keeps it in `exports/` of its state; the export leaves the outbox only then. The ledger copy goes at most once a day and with every full export, as for the repository. The owner reads exports back over REST (`src/supervisor/export-upload.ts`, `src/control/exports.ts`).
  - **"Have all results left this rig?"** `resultsLeft()` and `exportLeft()` in `src/control/results-left.ts`, for goal 023's terminate; also `GET /v1/rigs/<rig>/results-left`. A full reset now verifies its export on control for a rig without a results repository (builder's choice: the same check serves both).
  - The tunnel's route list (goal 019) takes the export and champion uploads.
  - Tests: `src/supervisor/model-download.test.ts`, `src/control/exports.test.ts`, `src/control/results-left.test.ts`. Pages: [Model files on a rig](../../_site/src/content/docs/reference/model-files.md), [Exports](../../_site/src/content/docs/reference/exports.md), [Bring a model's weights to a run](../../_site/src/content/docs/how-to/campaigns/model-weights.md), [Get a rig's results from control](../../_site/src/content/docs/how-to/operate/exports-on-control.md).
  - Still to do: a multi-GB model imported on a real rig (the tests stream 1 MB), and a terminated pod's champion found on control or in the repository, which needs goal 023's terminate.
- 2026-10-20 (goal 023): a RunPod pod's terminate now waits for `resultsLeft()` with its own full export, a champion's patch waiting included, and refuses when a result can never leave; a stop waits for it too, 15 minutes at most; a full reset of a RunPod rig waits for it as well as for its export. `scripts/runpod-acceptance.mjs` shows a terminate's full export on control before the pod goes. A champion from a real run on a terminated pod is still to show, in goal 025's paid run or a campaign on RunPod. Open for goals 020 and 022: put the inbox and the harness's state on the pod's volume, and get the Hugging Face token file to a pod without putting it in RunPod's settings.
- 2026-10-22: A multi-GB import on a rig of the real images: the compose stack (control and one rig), with the smoke campaign assigned through control and a 3 GiB model import (random bytes, so nothing could be compressed away) served over HTTP from the host. The supervisor fetched it in one request in about 24 seconds, sent nine progress reports to control (about every 3 seconds, from 129 MB to done), checked its SHA-256, and only then relayed the assignment. The harness accepted the assignment with the model, and the file in the inbox had the same SHA-256. A first try without the model in the contract was refused, as it should be: `model big-test is not listed in the contract`. Left: a terminated pod's champion on control, which the paid run of goal 025 shows (its smoke check makes a champion, and the terminate waits for every result to leave the pod).

